\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Believe not those who say
\par The upward path is smooth,
\par Lest thou shouldst stumble in the way
\par And faint before the truth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. It is the only road
\par Unto the realms of joy
\par But he who seeks that blest abode
\par Must all his powers employ.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Arm-arm thee for the fight!
\par Cast useless loads away;
\par Watch through the darkest hours of night;
\par Toil through the hottest
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To labour and to love,
\par To pardon and endure,
\par To lift thy heart to God
\par And keep thy concience ...
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Be this thy constant aim,
\par Thy hope, thy chief delight;
\par What matter who should whisper blame
\par Or who should scorn or slight:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. If but thy God approve,
\par And if, within thy breast,
\par Thou feel the comfort of His love,
\par The earnest of His rest.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

